cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  An Agentic LLM System for Anomaly Detection and Automated
  Resolution in Cold-Chain Logistics
message: If you use this software or its results, please cite the paper.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Mohammad
    family-names: Salahuddin
    email: fttf8892@leeds.ac.uk
    affiliation: University of Leeds
    orcid:
repository-code: "https://github.com/mohammadsalahuddinanwer/agentic-cold-chain"
abstract: >-
  An agentic, LLM-powered multi-agent system that detects, diagnoses and
  resolves cold-chain temperature anomalies. Evaluated with an event-based
  protocol in which detection lead time is measured rather than assumed,
  false alarms are costed, and conditions share common random numbers
  across ten seeds. The measured saving is attributed to automated
  resolution rather than to proactive detection or LLM reasoning.
keywords:
  - agentic AI
  - large language models
  - multi-agent systems
  - cold-chain logistics
  - anomaly detection
  - retrieval-augmented generation
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-03"
